  "note": "A2 liść · the payoff for a2_dat_chunks. POOL-CHECKED against end-of-a2_dat_chunks: apteka, tabletka, lekarstwo, zdrowie, boleć, temperatura, gorączka, kaszel, przeziębienie, grypa, lekarz, szpital, wizyta, dentysta are ALL already owned by a1_health and are ANCHORS here, never re-taught. plecy is already owned by a1_body (gender pl) — also an anchor, not re-taught. 12 genuinely new words: katar, gardło, alergia, syrop, recepta, plaster, termometr, przychodnia, badanie, szczepienie, ubezpieczenie, ciśnienie. umówić się DROPPED — perfective, and the batch is imperfective-only. BOLĄ: a2_dat_chunks fenced out plural subjects, so boli was the only form Dad has. This pack deliberately opens that one crack and no more — bolą is taught as the plural twin inside the same frozen block (bolą mnie plecy / bolą mnie nogi), tagged in teaches_lemmas, with no paradigm, no other verb, and no new structure id. It is safe because plecy and nogi are both already taught, so each of those sentences still has exactly ONE unknown: the form bolą. The -ENIE FAMILY is the quiet pattern of this unit: badanie, szczepienie, ubezpieczenie, ciśnienie all end in -enie and are all neuter, and Dad already has przeziębienie from A1 — so the gender is predictable rather than four separate facts. Accusative surfaces receptę and alergię appear in sentences, so they are taught as whole mam-phrases in the third block and tagged. Tone is everyday-ailment only: a cold, a sore throat, a plaster, a free flu jab, a routine check-up. No serious illness anywhere.",
